WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.060
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.340 --> 01:24.070
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:30.490 --> 01:31.180
Wait!

01:31.790 --> 01:32.720
I'm sorry!

01:35.490 --> 01:37.690
Please forgive your mother! I'm sorry!

01:50.510 --> 01:51.770
We were abandoned...

01:52.570 --> 01:54.740
We were abandoned by our parents!

01:55.210 --> 01:57.240
It's only Naoya and me now.

01:57.550 --> 01:59.210
We were abandoned!

02:00.820 --> 02:02.120
<i>Reminiscence</i>

02:02.120 --> 02:05.920
<i>Reminiscence
Episode 5</i>

02:20.440 --> 02:22.430
Naoto's in a good mood.

02:22.500 --> 02:26.800
It's fine that he's energetic,
but Naoto breaks his toys so fast.

02:27.440 --> 02:30.000
Let him play with it as he likes.

02:30.180 --> 02:32.080
Plus they're samples
of our company's toys.

02:32.150 --> 02:35.010
Even if they break,
there are many other ones.

02:38.550 --> 02:41.520
But this one is well made.

03:14.490 --> 03:15.820
There's no battery in it!

03:16.090 --> 03:18.250
How was he moving it?

03:24.070 --> 03:24.930
Honey!

03:29.400 --> 03:30.740
You have a nosebleed.

03:36.110 --> 03:37.740
When I was a child...

03:38.080 --> 03:42.450
...I thought everyone could move
things without actually touching them.

03:45.050 --> 03:48.320
When I became 6 years old,
you were born.

03:49.660 --> 03:54.600
Our parents felt insecure with me,
so they were happy about your birth.

04:11.450 --> 04:12.070
It's an earthquake!

04:28.430 --> 04:29.260
Naoto!

04:30.330 --> 04:31.160
Are you okay?

04:31.800 --> 04:32.600
Naoya.

04:33.000 --> 04:33.970
Did you hit your head?

04:34.200 --> 04:35.290
You're not hurt are you?

04:38.370 --> 04:39.530
There, there.

04:44.180 --> 04:47.480
Don't worry. There's nothing
to be worried about.

04:50.090 --> 04:54.990
That was the voice of mother's
heart that you read off of her.

05:07.270 --> 05:10.570
Do you remember that incident?

05:12.370 --> 05:17.510
Father's old subordinate, Hanaoka,
came to sell some land.

05:17.950 --> 05:19.040
That incident.

05:20.180 --> 05:21.150
Yeah.

05:23.420 --> 05:28.620
With society's market price, essentially
this kind of price can't be thought of...

05:28.760 --> 05:33.750
...but we have a situation, and I can't
make our company's profit any higher.

05:33.900 --> 05:37.330
Please think of it as a
tax reduction counter-plan.

05:37.600 --> 05:42.830
Seriously, we have been taken
care of well from your father's era.

05:43.440 --> 05:49.000
Yes, that's why with this price we
wanted to hand it over to your company.

05:49.110 --> 05:52.310
So we brought this
straight to you, Kirihara-san.

05:55.350 --> 05:59.580
But even though it's cheap,
the price is still the price.

05:59.690 --> 06:01.590
Yes, of course.

06:01.860 --> 06:04.050
Please take your time
and think about it.

06:04.660 --> 06:07.150
I'm going to go talk
to Naoto and Naoya.

06:07.600 --> 06:09.150
Yes, go ahead.

06:29.580 --> 06:31.050
What were you guys looking at?

06:31.420 --> 06:34.450
You brothers are seriously gloomy.

06:35.660 --> 06:38.250
Just looking at you guys,
you piss me off!

06:51.440 --> 06:53.460
It's a mystery even
thinking about it now.

06:54.340 --> 06:58.540
Why were Mom and Dad almost
deceived by people like them.

06:59.080 --> 06:59.810
Yeah.

07:01.580 --> 07:06.380
When I saw those people, I had
this anxiety that I couldn't describe.

07:06.860 --> 07:07.690
Yeah.

07:10.490 --> 07:15.400
I seriously wanted to know what
was inside of those people's hearts.

07:15.630 --> 07:18.290
It was the first time I thought like that.

07:18.670 --> 07:20.260
Even though I was so scared...

07:21.770 --> 07:22.760
Please double check.

07:23.540 --> 07:24.530
Okay then.

07:30.510 --> 07:31.210
Surely.

07:32.010 --> 07:33.810
Thank you very much.

07:34.120 --> 07:36.140
Now the contract is complete.

07:36.380 --> 07:40.720
No, thank you for bringing
such a good deal to me.

07:40.990 --> 07:43.690
Well, we'll get going now.

07:43.990 --> 07:46.020
Why don't you stay for a drink?

07:46.430 --> 07:49.230
No, we're in a hurry. I'm sorry.

07:49.430 --> 07:50.190
Come on, let's go.

07:50.500 --> 07:51.230
Yes.

07:51.300 --> 07:52.100
Yes.

08:05.710 --> 08:07.410
Naoto, Naoya?

08:07.920 --> 08:08.880
What's the matter?

08:09.380 --> 08:12.440
Hey boys, we're in a hurry.

08:12.750 --> 08:14.280
Could you let us through?

08:30.610 --> 08:32.160
Bring more and more!

08:45.250 --> 08:46.150
Naoya!

08:46.620 --> 08:48.450
These guys are liars!

08:48.960 --> 08:52.390
They are deceiving dad and
trying to take the money!

08:52.460 --> 08:53.150
Naoya!

08:54.360 --> 08:56.260
What is the meaning of this?

08:56.400 --> 08:58.630
Come on, let's hurry and go.

08:58.800 --> 09:00.430
Yeah, l-let's do that.

09:00.540 --> 09:02.090
H-Hold on a second.

09:02.600 --> 09:04.500
Please let me see the
documents once more.

09:04.670 --> 09:06.300
O-Once more...

09:06.610 --> 09:08.970
The agreement has
already been settled!

09:09.240 --> 09:10.010
Let's go!

09:10.080 --> 09:10.980
You can't!

09:16.650 --> 09:17.810
What's with you!

09:17.890 --> 09:19.550
What did you do to my dad!

09:24.790 --> 09:26.760
Sanae, what's wrong!

09:31.570 --> 09:32.900
Sanae!

09:34.200 --> 09:35.570
Help me!

09:35.640 --> 09:36.800
Naoto!

09:39.740 --> 09:44.010
Both of our powers
fully awakened after that.

09:45.050 --> 09:45.880
Yeah.

09:47.120 --> 09:48.670
But because of that...

09:49.080 --> 09:52.610
How mom and dad looked at us...

09:53.320 --> 09:55.720
...changed from the times before.

10:06.330 --> 10:07.820
The dollhouse.

10:08.200 --> 10:09.600
It's still here.

10:19.250 --> 10:23.210
A girl who never changed her
facial expression just like a doll...

10:23.450 --> 10:26.890
...lived with her father in this house.

10:34.800 --> 10:38.600
She was a girl that suffered from
a different kind of suffering than us.

10:39.430 --> 10:42.340
I think that was being conveyed to you.

10:43.810 --> 10:45.400
Those days...

10:45.470 --> 10:48.770
...you were terrified of
touching anybody but myself.

10:49.510 --> 10:51.030
As for myself...

10:56.250 --> 10:57.150
Naoto...

10:59.790 --> 11:03.380
You don't have to go to
school anymore starting today.

11:07.330 --> 11:08.300
It's because...

11:09.060 --> 11:11.190
...you injured people around you.

11:11.730 --> 11:15.100
We talked it over with the teachers,
and that's what was decided.

11:31.790 --> 11:32.780
Stop it, Naoto!

11:54.810 --> 11:55.470
Naoya?

12:08.490 --> 12:09.820
Naoya, no!

12:42.890 --> 12:44.150
Naoya, Naoya!

12:44.760 --> 12:47.460
Naoya, what's the matter?
Naoya, what did you see?

12:57.110 --> 12:59.670
Naoya has an illness, okay?

13:00.140 --> 13:02.770
If we don't cure him,
don't you feel bad?

13:03.340 --> 13:04.170
Right?

13:04.280 --> 13:05.710
Please understand, Naoto.

13:06.210 --> 13:09.050
You can't let people touch Naoya!

13:09.220 --> 13:10.480
Not even doctors!

13:10.850 --> 13:12.150
You can't!

13:17.890 --> 13:18.690
I'm sorry.

13:19.360 --> 13:21.590
I-I didn't mean...

13:31.010 --> 13:34.960
Have there been any other times
that Naoya-kun has become like this?

13:35.080 --> 13:36.200
Sometimes...

13:36.640 --> 13:40.170
...he'd get shocked so bad,
he'd get a fever.

13:40.680 --> 13:44.780
Really? In what kind of
situations was he shocked?

13:46.690 --> 13:48.280
Naoto, it's fine.

13:48.920 --> 13:50.290
You can say anything.

13:51.090 --> 13:52.250
When he...

13:52.460 --> 13:55.190
When he touches people
and sees bad things.

13:55.600 --> 13:57.330
What are bad things?

13:58.030 --> 13:59.290
Like lies...

13:59.930 --> 14:01.230
...and grudges.

14:01.870 --> 14:05.030
Naoya is able to read
what people are thinking.

14:05.310 --> 14:06.930
Especially when he touches them...

14:07.680 --> 14:08.870
Really.

14:09.040 --> 14:14.450
So Naoto-kun, how did you find out that
Naoya-kun is able to do these things?

14:15.420 --> 14:18.250
That's because Naoya says so.

14:18.990 --> 14:23.290
And what Naoya says is always right.

14:23.390 --> 14:24.380
Really?

14:26.230 --> 14:28.060
Is that so. I see.

14:29.030 --> 14:30.290
You're not surprised?

14:30.870 --> 14:32.590
Not with just that.

14:32.870 --> 14:38.310
Then why is Naoya-kun able to
read what people are thinking?

14:38.510 --> 14:41.410
That's because he
has that kind of power.

14:41.940 --> 14:43.710
What do you mean
by that kind of power?

14:43.780 --> 14:45.210
Of the mind...

14:46.610 --> 14:51.640
That's not something you can see,
but how do you know it's there?

14:53.290 --> 14:56.310
You can't see air,
but you know it's there, right?

14:56.490 --> 14:59.950
Air is scientifically proven to be there.

15:00.130 --> 15:04.330
But, a power to be able to
read someone's mind isn't...

15:04.400 --> 15:06.660
...something that can be proven, right?

15:06.970 --> 15:12.170
Maybe that was something your
brother made up and decided on?

15:13.810 --> 15:15.240
What we've decided...

15:15.580 --> 15:17.870
Are you saying we're lying?

15:18.480 --> 15:20.710
I'm not saying you're lying, but...

15:20.780 --> 15:22.870
...you don't like other
people butting into...

15:22.950 --> 15:28.120
...something that you brothers
have decided on together, right?

15:28.190 --> 15:29.710
I know how you feel.

15:30.360 --> 15:33.450
Listen up. Hurry and fix
Naoya back to normal!

15:37.270 --> 15:39.060
Naoto, stop.

15:39.500 --> 15:40.520
Please stop.

15:42.970 --> 15:45.300
I couldn't leave it up
to a doctor like that.

15:46.040 --> 15:49.030
I headed towards the dollhouse.

15:50.310 --> 15:55.680
I went to know what
you saw inside that girl.

16:37.190 --> 16:38.160
It hurts!

16:38.460 --> 16:40.190
Father, it hurts!

16:40.860 --> 16:41.760
Stop it!

16:42.700 --> 16:44.890
Father, stop!

16:47.300 --> 16:49.830
I am doing this for you.

16:50.140 --> 16:53.870
I want you to become a good girl,
so I give you pain.

17:26.140 --> 17:27.570
What are you doing...

17:27.640 --> 17:29.300
...in this place!

17:41.860 --> 17:43.020
This is awful.

17:44.030 --> 17:46.550
I'm going to untie you right now.

17:52.630 --> 17:53.930
W-Wait!

17:54.140 --> 17:54.900
Ayane!

17:56.740 --> 17:57.640
Help!

17:57.910 --> 17:58.960
Someone help!

18:01.110 --> 18:03.010
Please! Help!

18:05.910 --> 18:07.040
Wait!

18:07.210 --> 18:09.510
Return... Return Ayane!

18:13.050 --> 18:15.150
Police! Someone call the police!

18:42.120 --> 18:43.110
Naoya...

18:43.850 --> 18:45.820
Seriously, what happened to you?

18:47.720 --> 18:48.710
Naoya!

18:50.290 --> 18:51.950
Naoya! Can you hear me?

18:52.560 --> 18:54.530
That girl was saved.

18:54.860 --> 18:57.490
The police arrested that father.

18:57.830 --> 18:59.990
The girl was saved!

19:00.330 --> 19:02.030
So come back!

19:02.500 --> 19:04.490
Naoya, come back!

19:04.570 --> 19:05.330
Naoya!

19:21.020 --> 19:22.110
Brother...

19:22.460 --> 19:23.510
Naoya!

19:33.330 --> 19:37.240
Her father's abuse was so severe.

19:39.370 --> 19:43.740
Her father thought that that was
the way to express his love to her.

19:44.280 --> 19:45.610
By hurting her...

19:46.910 --> 19:50.780
But the human body
becomes wounded...

19:50.850 --> 19:55.080
...so he made a doll and
had it on display in a clean form.

19:56.460 --> 19:58.290
I wonder what happened to that girl.

19:58.460 --> 20:00.590
The wound she got from that
was most likely really deep.

20:01.330 --> 20:03.490
But now she should be...

20:04.500 --> 20:06.590
That doll was creepy.

20:07.670 --> 20:09.760
I still remember those red eyes.

20:10.440 --> 20:11.960
What? Red?

20:12.740 --> 20:13.600
Yeah.

20:15.810 --> 20:19.250
I saw that doll in
the girl's consciousness.

20:19.780 --> 20:21.300
It had blue eyes.

20:23.450 --> 20:25.510
No, it was red.

20:30.090 --> 20:31.060
Well, whatever.

20:31.630 --> 20:33.060
It's all over with.

20:34.330 --> 20:35.760
Let's go, Naoya.

20:36.400 --> 20:37.560
To see our house...

20:39.200 --> 20:39.830
Brother...

20:40.770 --> 20:41.530
What?

20:41.700 --> 20:43.230
I'm kind of scared.

20:44.000 --> 20:45.730
I'm scared to go to our house.

21:18.170 --> 21:18.970
It's not here.

21:19.810 --> 21:21.140
Our house isn't here.

21:21.910 --> 21:23.310
What is the meaning of this?

21:24.950 --> 21:26.340
Um, excuse me.

21:26.810 --> 21:27.780
Yes?

21:28.620 --> 21:31.950
The house that used to be here...
When was it taken down?

21:32.490 --> 21:33.380
A house?

21:33.890 --> 21:35.450
In this empty lot...

21:35.720 --> 21:36.350
A house?

21:36.890 --> 21:40.880
This lot has been
empty since I was born.

21:41.460 --> 21:43.690
There's never been a house built here.

21:46.400 --> 21:47.770
That can't be...

21:55.340 --> 21:58.110
That girl that saved me...

22:29.910 --> 22:38.720
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:47.560
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

22:47.630 --> 22:56.400
<i>A single shadow looked like light
in this world that I'm imprisoned in.</i>

22:56.470 --> 23:05.210
<i>The rain of May became lighter
as it was kindly shining tomorrow.</i>

23:05.280 --> 23:09.610
<i>I lost the meaning of smiling...</i>

23:09.680 --> 23:13.980
<i>... that day I thought I
lost my place to be.</i>

23:14.050 --> 23:18.420
<i>I wished for your warmth.</i>

23:18.490 --> 23:22.930
<i>We have stopped time.</i>

23:23.160 --> 23:27.260
<i>I had this feeling it was
eventually going to come, but...</i>

23:27.330 --> 23:31.900
<i>... I pretended I didn't know
and buried my loneliness.</i>

23:31.970 --> 23:42.080
<i>I looked down at your feet as the
droplets describing "Good-bye" fell.</i>

23:42.720 --> 23:51.450
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

23:51.530 --> 23:59.900
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

24:02.500 --> 24:05.900
The reality that something
that should exist doesn't.

24:07.780 --> 24:11.340
Answering our own question that
gets repeated over and over.

24:12.910 --> 24:17.320
As we search for an unreliable answer
called the "truth," we turn our feet...

24:18.250 --> 24:21.050
...towards something enlarged
by the negative consciousness...

24:21.160 --> 24:22.950
...and that we can
learn from each other.

24:23.820 --> 24:29.860
<i>Episode 6, "Connection."</i>

24:26.360 --> 24:29.160
Where are we headed?
